Read the iOS and Android rules — key points I'm applying: 48dp/44pt minimum touch targets on rows, native confirmation dialogs (not a custom modal) for the destructive action, safe-area/inset-aware layout, Dynamic Type-friendly text (no truncation of primary labels), and RTL-safe `flex-start/end` instead of hardcoded left/right. Here's the screen:

```tsx
// AccountSettingsScreen.tsx
import React, { useCallback, useState } from 'react';
import {
  View,
  Text,
  StyleSheet,
  Pressable,
  Switch,
  Alert,
  ScrollView,
  Image,
  Platform,
} from 'react-native';
import { useSafeAreaInsets } from 'react-native-safe-area-context';

// ---- Design tokens -------------------------------------------------------
// Minimal, platform-aware tokens. Swap for your app's real theme/colors.
const colors = {
  background: '#FFFFFF',
  surface: '#FFFFFF',
  separator: Platform.select({ ios: '#E5E5EA', android: '#E0E0E0', default: '#E5E5EA' }),
  label: '#111111',
  secondaryLabel: '#6B6B6F',
  destructive: Platform.select({ ios: '#FF3B30', android: '#B3261E', default: '#D32F2F' }),
  ripple: 'rgba(0,0,0,0.08)',
};

// Minimum touch target: 44pt (iOS) / 48dp (Android) — 48 covers both.
const MIN_TOUCH_TARGET = 48;

// ---- Types ----------------------------------------------------------------
type NavigationRow = {
  type: 'navigation';
  key: string;
  label: string;
  value?: string;
  onPress: () => void;
};

type ToggleRow = {
  type: 'toggle';
  key: string;
  label: string;
  value: boolean;
  onValueChange: (next: boolean) => void;
};

type SettingsRowConfig = NavigationRow | ToggleRow;

interface Profile {
  name: string;
  email: string;
  avatarUri?: string;
}

// ---- Profile row ------------------------------------------------------------
function ProfileRow({ profile, onPress }: { profile: Profile; onPress: () => void }) {
  const initials = profile.name
    .split(' ')
    .map((p) => p[0])
    .slice(0, 2)
    .join('')
    .toUpperCase();

  return (
    <Pressable
      onPress={onPress}
      accessibilityRole="button"
      accessibilityLabel={`${profile.name}, ${profile.email}. View profile`}
      android_ripple={{ color: colors.ripple }}
      style={({ pressed }) => [
        styles.profileRow,
        Platform.OS === 'ios' && pressed && { opacity: 0.6 },
      ]}
    >
      {profile.avatarUri ? (
        <Image source={{ uri: profile.avatarUri }} style={styles.avatar} />
      ) : (
        <View style={[styles.avatar, styles.avatarFallback]}>
          <Text style={styles.avatarInitials} allowFontScaling={false}>
            {initials}
          </Text>
        </View>
      )}

      <View style={styles.profileText}>
        <Text style={styles.profileName} numberOfLines={2}>
          {profile.name}
        </Text>
        <Text style={styles.profileEmail} numberOfLines={1} ellipsizeMode="middle">
          {profile.email}
        </Text>
      </View>

      <Chevron />
    </Pressable>
  );
}

// ---- Generic settings row ----------------------------------------------------
function SettingsRow({ row, isLast }: { row: SettingsRowConfig; isLast: boolean }) {
  if (row.type === 'toggle') {
    return (
      <View
        style={[styles.row, !isLast && styles.rowDivider]}
        accessible
        accessibilityRole="switch"
        accessibilityLabel={row.label}
        accessibilityState={{ checked: row.value }}
      >
        <Text style={styles.rowLabel}>{row.label}</Text>
        <Switch value={row.value} onValueChange={row.onValueChange} />
      </View>
    );
  }

  return (
    <Pressable
      onPress={row.onPress}
      accessibilityRole="button"
      accessibilityLabel={row.value ? `${row.label}, ${row.value}` : row.label}
      android_ripple={{ color: colors.ripple }}
      style={({ pressed }) => [
        styles.row,
        !isLast && styles.rowDivider,
        Platform.OS === 'ios' && pressed && { backgroundColor: colors.ripple },
      ]}
    >
      <Text style={styles.rowLabel} numberOfLines={2}>
        {row.label}
      </Text>
      <View style={styles.rowTrailing}>
        {row.value ? (
          <Text style={styles.rowValue} numberOfLines={1}>
            {row.value}
          </Text>
        ) : null}
        <Chevron />
      </View>
    </Pressable>
  );
}

function Chevron() {
  // Simple text glyph to avoid an icon-library dependency; mirrors for RTL automatically
  // because it sits in a flex-start/flex-end row rather than fixed left/right.
  return <Text style={styles.chevron}>{'\u203A'}</Text>;
}

function SectionHeader({ title }: { title: string }) {
  return <Text style={styles.sectionHeader}>{title}</Text>;
}

function Section({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return <View style={styles.section}>{children}</View>;
}

// ---- Screen ---------------------------------------------------------------
export default function AccountSettingsScreen() {
  const insets = useSafeAreaInsets();

  const [profile] = useState<Profile>({
    name: 'Jordan Rivera',
    email: 'jordan.rivera@example.com',
  });

  const [notificationsEnabled, setNotificationsEnabled] = useState(true);
  const [faceUnlockEnabled, setFaceUnlockEnabled] = useState(false);
  const [isDeleting, setIsDeleting] = useState(false);

  const handleEditProfile = useCallback(() => {
    // navigation.navigate('EditProfile')
  }, []);

  const handleDeleteAccount = useCallback(() => {
    // Native confirmation dialog on both platforms: iOS renders a destructive-styled
    // UIAlertController, Android renders a two-action Material dialog. Matches the
    // platform rule that an irreversible action needs an explicit, interruptive confirm.
    Alert.alert(
      'Delete account?',
      'This permanently deletes your account and all associated data. This action cannot be undone.',
      [
        { text: 'Cancel', style: 'cancel' },
        {
          text: 'Delete Account',
          style: 'destructive',
          onPress: () => {
            setIsDeleting(true);
            // deleteAccount().finally(() => setIsDeleting(false));
          },
        },
      ],
      { cancelable: true },
    );
  }, []);

  const accountRows: SettingsRowConfig[] = [
    { type: 'navigation', key: 'personal-info', label: 'Personal information', onPress: () => {} },
    { type: 'navigation', key: 'password', label: 'Password & security', onPress: () => {} },
    {
      type: 'navigation',
      key: 'email',
      label: 'Email address',
      value: profile.email,
      onPress: () => {},
    },
  ];

  const preferenceRows: SettingsRowConfig[] = [
    {
      type: 'toggle',
      key: 'notifications',
      label: 'Push notifications',
      value: notificationsEnabled,
      onValueChange: setNotificationsEnabled,
    },
    {
      type: 'toggle',
      key: 'biometrics',
      label: Platform.OS === 'ios' ? 'Face ID unlock' : 'Fingerprint unlock',
      value: faceUnlockEnabled,
      onValueChange: setFaceUnlockEnabled,
    },
    { type: 'navigation', key: 'language', label: 'Language', value: 'English', onPress: () => {} },
  ];

  const supportRows: SettingsRowConfig[] = [
    { type: 'navigation', key: 'help', label: 'Help & support', onPress: () => {} },
    { type: 'navigation', key: 'privacy', label: 'Privacy policy', onPress: () => {} },
    { type: 'navigation', key: 'about', label: 'About', value: 'v1.0.0', onPress: () => {} },
  ];

  return (
    <View style={[styles.screen, { paddingTop: insets.top }]}>
      <ScrollView
        contentContainerStyle={{ paddingBottom: insets.bottom + 24 }}
        contentInsetAdjustmentBehavior="automatic"
      >
        <Text style={styles.screenTitle}>Account</Text>

        <Section>
          <ProfileRow profile={profile} onPress={handleEditProfile} />
        </Section>

        <SectionHeader title="ACCOUNT" />
        <Section>
          {accountRows.map((row, i) => (
            <SettingsRow key={row.key} row={row} isLast={i === accountRows.length - 1} />
          ))}
        </Section>

        <SectionHeader title="PREFERENCES" />
        <Section>
          {preferenceRows.map((row, i) => (
            <SettingsRow key={row.key} row={row} isLast={i === preferenceRows.length - 1} />
          ))}
        </Section>

        <SectionHeader title="SUPPORT" />
        <Section>
          {supportRows.map((row, i) => (
            <SettingsRow key={row.key} row={row} isLast={i === supportRows.length - 1} />
          ))}
        </Section>

        <Pressable
          onPress={handleDeleteAccount}
          disabled={isDeleting}
          accessibilityRole="button"
          accessibilityLabel="Delete account"
          accessibilityHint="Opens a confirmation dialog before permanently deleting your account"
          android_ripple={{ color: colors.ripple }}
          style={({ pressed }) => [
            styles.deleteRow,
            isDeleting && { opacity: 0.5 },
            Platform.OS === 'ios' && pressed && { opacity: 0.6 },
          ]}
        >
          <Text style={styles.deleteLabel}>
            {isDeleting ? 'Deleting account…' : 'Delete account'}
          </Text>
        </Pressable>
      </ScrollView>
    </View>
  );
}

// ---- Styles -----------------------------------------------------------------
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  screen: {
    flex: 1,
    backgroundColor: colors.background,
  },
  screenTitle: {
    fontSize: 28,
    fontWeight: '700',
    color: colors.label,
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
    paddingTop: 8,
    paddingBottom: 12,
  },
  section: {
    backgroundColor: colors.surface,
    borderTopWidth: 1,
    borderBottomWidth: 1,
    borderColor: colors.separator,
  },
  sectionHeader: {
    fontSize: 13,
    fontWeight: '600',
    color: colors.secondaryLabel,
    textTransform: 'uppercase',
    letterSpacing: 0.4,
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
    paddingTop: 20,
    paddingBottom: 6,
  },
  profileRow: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
    minHeight: 72, // larger than the 48 floor since this row carries primary identity info
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
    paddingVertical: 12,
  },
  avatar: {
    width: 48,
    height: 48,
    borderRadius: 24,
  },
  avatarFallback: {
    backgroundColor: colors.separator,
    justifyContent: 'center',
    alignItems: 'center',
  },
  avatarInitials: {
    fontSize: 16,
    fontWeight: '600',
    color: colors.label,
  },
  profileText: {
    flex: 1,
    marginStart: 12,
    marginEnd: 8,
  },
  profileName: {
    fontSize: 17,
    fontWeight: '600',
    color: colors.label,
  },
  profileEmail: {
    fontSize: 14,
    color: colors.secondaryLabel,
    marginTop: 2,
  },
  row: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
    justifyContent: 'space-between',
    minHeight: MIN_TOUCH_TARGET,
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
    paddingVertical: 8,
  },
  rowDivider: {
    borderBottomWidth: 1,
    borderColor: colors.separator,
  },
  rowLabel: {
    fontSize: 16,
    color: colors.label,
    flexShrink: 1,
    marginEnd: 12,
  },
  rowTrailing: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
  },
  rowValue: {
    fontSize: 16,
    color: colors.secondaryLabel,
    marginEnd: 4,
    maxWidth: 140,
  },
  chevron: {
    fontSize: 20,
    color: colors.secondaryLabel,
    transform: [{ scaleX: 1 }], // RN mirrors this automatically under RTL layout
  },
  deleteRow: {
    minHeight: MIN_TOUCH_TARGET,
    justifyContent: 'center',
    alignItems: 'center',
    marginTop: 32,
    marginHorizontal: 16,
  },
  deleteLabel: {
    fontSize: 16,
    fontWeight: '600',
    color: colors.destructive,
  },
});
```

Notes on the platform decisions baked in (not just styling preference):

- **Confirmation uses `Alert.alert`, not a custom modal.** It's the one destructive action on the screen with no triggering control to anchor an action sheet to, and it needs to interrupt — exactly what both HIGs reserve alerts/dialogs for. On iOS it renders a destructive-styled system alert; on Android, a two-action Material dialog (confirm vs. dismiss) — each platform gets its native look for free.
- **Touch targets** are `minHeight: 48` on every row (covers iOS's 44pt and Android's 48dp floor), with the profile row intentionally taller since it's the primary identity control.
- **Text isn't truncated where it matters**: profile name wraps instead of clipping (`numberOfLines={2}`, no `ellipsizeMode`) so long names survive Dynamic Type / large font scale; only the secondary email and row-value strings use `ellipsizeMode`.
- **RTL-safe layout**: `marginStart/marginEnd` instead of `marginLeft/marginRight`, and the chevron direction is left to RN's automatic mirroring rather than a hardcoded icon.
- **`useSafeAreaInsets`** (from `react-native-safe-area-context`, the de facto standard for this — add it if not already a dependency) handles the status bar/notch on iOS and edge-to-edge insets on Android instead of RN core's iOS-only `SafeAreaView`.
- **Ripple vs. opacity feedback** is split per platform (`android_ripple` vs. a manual pressed-opacity style) so each OS gets its native press affordance instead of one borrowed from the other.

One assumption I made explicit rather than silent: I used `react-native-safe-area-context` for insets since RN's built-in `SafeAreaView` doesn't work on Android — swap it out if your app already standardizes on something else.
